hcobb <henry.cobb@gmail.com> wrote:
> It sounds to me as if you are not advancing your equipment to match
> your level so you get nasties that you can't handle.

Agreed. I don't use a fixed ratio of dungeon level to experience level;
balance is more fluid (and depends on more factors) than that. I don't
do the protection racket; generally I dive for Sokoban first, for food
and the gift.

As you mentioned, unless you have a =oSD to take the pressure off, food
will compel you to keep going lower (especially if you're toting a
starting pet, which will need to eat). But I will wear every piece of
armor I find that my pet will step on. As Henry says, above, AC is at
least as important as XL as the monsters get tougher.

If the Sokoban entrance is deep, then I just have to watch my context.
The less armor I've found and the fewer XL I've gained, the more
cautious I have to be, and the more ready to beat a hasty retreat. If I
just can't reach it, I'll abandon the Sokoban dive for Minetown, which
is higher up. Either way, Mines or Sokoban, I'll generally get to XL9
and AC:0 or so, and at that point, I can descend as each level is
cleared without worrying.

